# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository *and* in the working tree,
# including on Windows.
#
# Windows CI runners (GitHub Actions, R-hub) check out with core.autocrlf=true,
# which rewrites the autoconf inputs and the C sources to CRLF.  R CMD check
# then reports, e.g.:
#
#   * checking line endings in shell scripts ... WARNING
#     Found the following shell script(s) with CR or CRLF line endings:
#       configure.ac
#     Non-Windows OSes require LF line endings.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf, so the checked-out bytes match what is
# committed here.  R CMD build drops .gitattributes from the tarball, so this
# file never reaches CRAN.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Recorded container build logs contain bare CR from progress output; keep them
# byte-for-byte rather than renormalizing them.
docker/**/logs/** -text

# Never touch binary payloads (text=auto already detects these, but be explicit
# so a stray edit to the rules above cannot corrupt the test fixtures).
*.h5  binary
*.png binary
